2026-06-25 11:53:51,647 | AGENT | ProjectCoordinator Agent answered: As the Project Coordinator at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I would coordinate the deployment of the solution by following our typical delivery structure, which includes phases such as Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support. Given the project's duration of 4 years and the requirement for a progressive deployment with a pilot phase, we would start by designing the solution in the first phase, followed by a pilot rollout to test and refine the solution.

To ensure the quality of service, we would establish a steering committee and implement our governance tools, including a RAID log, Decision log, and Change request process. We would also conduct regular status updates, with a weekly status report, monthly steering committee meetings, and quarterly executive reviews.

For the accompaniment to change and training actions for the agents, our dedicated change manager would provide training delivery through in-person workshops, e-learning, and quick reference guides. We track user adoption, and our typical training days per user are 0.5 days. This would help ensure that the agents are well-equipped to use the new solution and minimize any disruption during the transition period.

Throughout the project, we would maintain a risk register and review it bi-weekly, categorizing risks into technical, financial, regulatory, operational, and reputational categories. Our risk appetite is low-to-medium, and we would work closely with the client to identify and mitigate any potential risks that may arise during the deployment.

By following our established project management capabilities, including PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies, and leveraging our experience in leading consortia and managing large projects, we believe we can successfully coordinate the deployment of the solution, ensure the quality of service, and provide the necessary support to the agents during the transition period.
