2026-06-25 11:57:20,809 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: Our consortium proposes an artificial intelligence-based assistance system designed to improve the efficiency of administrative services and the quality of service rendered to users in the City of Belval. The intelligent assistance tool will accompany agents in their administrative activities, assisting with tasks such as searching for information in internal procedures and applicable regulations, drafting letters or answers to users, and suggesting actions or steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process.

The solution integrates with existing practices of agents and does not constitute a rupture in their modes of work. It achieves contextualization of answers in function of the demand of the agent, proposes help with the drafting of administrative contents, such as answers to users, administrative letters, and syntheses of files, and recalls applicable rules. The system also suggests actions or verifications to carry out and facilitates the continuity of the processing of files between agents and services.

Our proposed technical architecture uses AI/ML systems, cloud architecture, API integration, data engineering, and cybersecurity. The solution leverages large language models, retrieval-augmented generation, and explainability methods to provide intelligent assistance and improve answer quality. It reduces processing time and provides transparent and interpretable results.

The system is deployed on cloud infrastructure using OVHCloud, Scaleway, Outscale, SecNumCloud, or Azure EU regions, with a deployment strategy that includes Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), Helm, and API gateways such as Kong, Apigee, or AWS API Gateway. The solution complies with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and ensures data sovereignty by hosting data in the European Union.

Our approach optimizes costs, guarantees quality of service, and minimizes environmental impact by reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructure with low carbon impact. We provide training delivery through in-person workshops, e-learning, and quick reference guides, as well as change management support during the transition period.

The project has a global budget of 3 million euros, a duration of four years, and an annual cost of exploitation compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. Our solution includes an accompaniment to change and actions of training for the agents, ensuring a smooth transition and minimizing disruption.

We guarantee a high level of availability, with 99.9% uptime, and ensure that our system integrates with existing systems of information, including civil status, town planning, electronic management of documents (EDM), and user directories. Our team has experience in managing large projects, leading consortia, and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.

Our proposal includes a pilot phase on a limited scope followed by a progressive generalization to all services, with regular status updates, weekly status reports, monthly steering committee meetings, and quarterly executive reviews. We track user adoption and provide risk mitigation strategies to ensure the success of the project.

In conclusion, our consortium offers a comprehensive solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence-based assistance system, ensuring improved efficiency, quality of service, and compliance with regulatory requirements while minimizing environmental impact.
